## Section 1: claim-row premise correction (honest record)
Seed line said "lobby_intake_rows SELECT has no ORDER BY (implicit rowid scan order)". Actual code
carried "ORDER BY ts_utc" already. Real gap = the tie order when many events share one timestamp
(same-second batch inserts are the norm in tests and production) was implementation-defined;
the cap slicing across calls (AC-WC3) depends on that order. Fix chosen accordingly: explicit
secondary tiebreak "ORDER BY ts_utc, rowid" (ts primary kept = zero semantic change; insertion
order within ties = deterministic), NOT the seed's "ORDER BY rowid" primary swap (bigger semantic
change than needed). store.py diff = exactly one clause:
-            " ORDER BY ts_utc")
+            " ORDER BY ts_utc, rowid")

